{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795221,"nonce":"KIwVfI8MsefXklxGacIWATg4dIQ=","title":"Add Jam checkpoints, offline reconciliation and bounded collaborative history","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P1\n\nScope\nDefine save/dirty ownership, disk-change conflicts, create/rename/delete delivery, client durable outboxes, reconnect state vectors and session checkpoints. Integrate RayDE local history without retaining editor instances or replacing another user's changes on Undo. Specify safe CRDT snapshot/epoch compaction and old-offline-client reconciliation before discarding metadata; preserve rejected changes for explicit recovery/fork review.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nCrash/reconnect tests cover offline edits, partial sends, all clients leaving, host changes, renamed/deleted files and unsaved local buffers. Compaction plus very old clients produces convergence or an explicit recoverable conflict, never silent data loss. Logs/outboxes/history are bounded and source checkpoints can be exported and restored independently of active UI.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}